From 9c0e289b4696904c854e65f3d4971fda6c1d9c3d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Emil J. Tywoniak" <emil@tywoniak.eu>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 02:39:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 17/18] anv: program the full HEVC LCU max bit size on Gfx12.5+

lcu_max_bits_size_allowed() needs up to 18 bits (81920 for 8 bit 4:2:0
with 64x64 CTBs) but was masked to 16, so the PAK got 16384. From
Gfx12.5 on HCP_PIC_STATE carries the two MSBs in DW6 bits 18:17, like
the media driver programs them (LcuMaxBitSizeAllowedMsb2its in the
Xe_HPM and Xe2 HCP definitions). Add the field to the Gfx12.5 genxml and
program it.

No visible change in output with the LCU max size report disabled, but
the value is no longer bogus if that is turned on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014zf3d6ZuUHNvTB81JRfHds
